# Paths excluded from `rg`, and therefore from most editor and agent search.
#
# Four upstream C libraries are vendored under crates/ so the FFI wrappers can
# build them: 2,021 tracked files, roughly three times the size of SonicTerm's
# own source. An unfiltered search for anything generic — `buffer`, `size`,
# `error` — returns mostly FreeType and HarfBuzz, which buries the first-party
# hit that was being looked for.
#
# These are still tracked, still built, and still greppable when needed:
# `rg --no-ignore <pattern> crates/sonicterm-freetype/freetype2` searches them
# explicitly. This file only changes the default.
#
# Note: git itself ignores this file. `git grep` and `git ls-files` continue to
# see everything, which is what makes them the right tool when the question is
# "what does the repository contain" rather than "where is our code".

crates/sonicterm-freetype/freetype2/
crates/sonicterm-freetype/libpng/
crates/sonicterm-freetype/zlib/
crates/sonicterm-harfbuzz/harfbuzz/

# Build output and packaging artifacts.
target/
dist/

# Ripgrep skips dot-directories by default, which hides `.github/` — the CI
# workflows, issue templates, and dependabot config. Those are first-party
# files someone editing CI needs to find by searching for them, so un-hide
# that one tree. Everything else dot-prefixed stays hidden.
!.github/
